From aa1e3b6825f3260fc471c48c669f0fbc68ff3278 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 22:48:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(migrate): auto-import Beads on first kernel use so
 upgraded repos keep their issues

The kernel is the default backend, but onboarding auto-migrate runs only from
setup/init. An existing repo whose user merely upgrades forge would read an empty
kernel on the first issue command and their existing issues would appear to vanish
(data safe in the jsonl store, but no hint).

Add a one-time runtime auto-migrate hook in resolveCommandOpts (kernel path):
gated by a sentinel next to the kernel DB (shared across worktrees), idempotent via
autoMigrateBeadsIfPresent, stderr-only so --json stdout stays a pure contract. Falls
back to a one-line nudge on import failure. A store with no jsonl export is skipped
silently (no false positive on an empty leftover dir). Regenerate the D20 kill-list
artifact (line-number shift only; zero new bd/dolt references).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
